msgid "Cube 算子开发"
msgstr "Cube operator development"

msgid "Cube 算子以矩阵乘或批量矩阵乘为主要计算负载，Triton 代码中通常以 `tl.dot` 为核心。Cube 算子的关键是围绕 M/N/K 三个维度设计 tile，使 A/B tile 能高效搬运到片上并在 Cube Core 上完成累加。"
msgstr "Cube operators use matrix multiplication or batch matrix multiplication as the primary computational load. In Triton code, `tl.dot` is typically the core. The key to Cube operators is designing tiles around the three dimensions: M, N, and K. This enables the A and B tiles to be efficiently moved to the on-chip memory and accumulated on the Cube Core."

msgid "Cube 简单算子开发"
msgstr "Cube Simple Operator Development"

msgid "简单 Cube 算子可参考本仓 [矩阵乘法样例](../examples/05_matrix_multiplication_example.md)。一个最小开发路径包括："
msgstr "For simple Cube operators, refer to the [Matrix Multiplication sample](../examples/05_matrix_multiplication_example.md) in this repository. A minimal development path includes:"

msgid "明确输入输出 shape 和 stride，例如 `A[M, K]`、`B[K, N]`、`C[M, N]`。"
msgstr "Clearly define the input and output shapes and strides, for example, `A[M, K]`, `B[K, N]`, `C[M, N]`."

msgid "用 `tl.program_id` 映射当前 program 到输出矩阵的 `(pid_m, pid_n)` tile。"
msgstr "Map the current program to the `(pid_m, pid_n)` tile of the output matrix using `tl.program_id`."

msgid "用 `BLOCK_SIZE_M/N/K` 构造 A/B 的二维偏移。"
msgstr "Construct the 2D offsets for A/B using `BLOCK_SIZE_M/N/K`."

msgid "沿 K 维循环加载 A/B 子块，并用 `tl.dot` 累加到 fp32 accumulator。"
msgstr "Load A/B sub-blocks cyclically along the K dimension and accumulate them into the fp32 accumulator using `tl.dot`."

msgid "将 accumulator 转为输出 dtype，并用边界 mask 写回 C。"
msgstr "Cast the accumulator to the output dtype and write back to C using the boundary mask."

msgid "核心结构如下："
msgstr "The core structure is as follows:"

msgid ""
"@triton.jit\n"
"def matmul_kernel(a_ptr, b_ptr, c_ptr,\n"
"                  M: tl.constexpr, N: tl.constexpr, K: tl.constexpr,\n"
"                  stride_am: tl.constexpr, stride_ak: tl.constexpr,\n"
"                  stride_bk: tl.constexpr, stride_bn: tl.constexpr,\n"
"                  stride_cm: tl.constexpr, stride_cn: tl.constexpr,\n"
"                  BLOCK_M: tl.constexpr, BLOCK_N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK_K: tl.constexpr):\n"
"    pid = tl.program_id(0)\n"
"    num_pid_n = tl.cdiv(N, BLOCK_N)\n"
"    pid_m = pid // num_pid_n\n"
"    pid_n = pid % num_pid_n\n"
"\n"
"    offs_m = pid_m * BLOCK_M + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_M)\n"
"    offs_n = pid_n * BLOCK_N + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_N)\n"
"    offs_k = tl.arange(0, BLOCK_K)\n"
"    acc = tl.zeros((BLOCK_M, BLOCK_N), dtype=tl.float32)\n"
"\n"
"    for k0 in range(0, K, BLOCK_K):\n"
"        a = tl.load(a_ptr + offs_m[:, None] * stride_am + (k0 + offs_k)[None, :] * stride_ak,\n"
"                    mask=(offs_m[:, None] < M) & ((k0 + offs_k)[None, :] < K), other=0.0)\n"
"        b = tl.load(b_ptr + (k0 + offs_k)[:, None] * stride_bk + offs_n[None, :] * stride_bn,\n"
"                    mask=((k0 + offs_k)[:, None] < K) & (offs_n[None, :] < N), other=0.0)\n"
"        acc = tl.dot(a, b, acc)\n"
"\n"
"    tl.store(c_ptr + offs_m[:, None] * stride_cm + offs_n[None, :] * stride_cn,\n"
"             acc, mask=(offs_m[:, None] < M) & (offs_n[None, :] < N))\n"
msgstr ""
"@triton.jit\n"
"def matmul_kernel(a_ptr, b_ptr, c_ptr,\n"
"                  M: tl.constexpr, N: tl.constexpr, K: tl.constexpr,\n"
"                  stride_am: tl.constexpr, stride_ak: tl.constexpr,\n"
"                  stride_bk: tl.constexpr, stride_bn: tl.constexpr,\n"
"                  stride_cm: tl.constexpr, stride_cn: tl.constexpr,\n"
"                  BLOCK_M: tl.constexpr, BLOCK_N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK_K: tl.constexpr):\n"
"    pid = tl.program_id(0)\n"
"    num_pid_n = tl.cdiv(N, BLOCK_N)\n"
"    pid_m = pid // num_pid_n\n"
"    pid_n = pid % num_pid_n\n"
"\n"
"    offs_m = pid_m * BLOCK_M + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_M)\n"
"    offs_n = pid_n * BLOCK_N + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_N)\n"
"    offs_k = tl.arange(0, BLOCK_K)\n"
"    acc = tl.zeros((BLOCK_M, BLOCK_N), dtype=tl.float32)\n"
"\n"
"    for k0 in range(0, K, BLOCK_K):\n"
"        a = tl.load(a_ptr + offs_m[:, None] * stride_am + (k0 + offs_k)[None, :] * stride_ak,\n"
"                    mask=(offs_m[:, None] < M) & ((k0 + offs_k)[None, :] < K), other=0.0)\n"
"        b = tl.load(b_ptr + (k0 + offs_k)[:, None] * stride_bk + offs_n[None, :] * stride_bn,\n"
"                    mask=((k0 + offs_k)[:, None] < K) & (offs_n[None, :] < N), other=0.0)\n"
"        acc = tl.dot(a, b, acc)\n"
"\n"
"    tl.store(c_ptr + offs_m[:, None] * stride_cm + offs_n[None, :] * stride_cn,\n"
"             acc, mask=(offs_m[:, None] < M) & (offs_n[None, :] < N))\n"

msgid "简单 Cube 算子调参时优先关注："
msgstr "When tuning parameters for a simple Cube operator, prioritize attention to:"

msgid "`BLOCK_M/N/K` 是否满足硬件支持和 UB/L1 容量限制。"
msgstr "Whether `BLOCK_M/N/K` satisfies hardware support and UB/L1 capacity constraints."

msgid "K 维循环是否可以开启 `multibuffer` 以形成搬运和计算流水。"
msgstr "Can the K-dimension loop enable `multibuffer` to form a pipeline of data movement and computation?"

msgid "输出 tile 是否包含额外 bias、scale、activation。如果后处理很轻，可以仍归为 Cube 算子；如果后处理包含明显 Vector 归约或跨核同步，应按 CV 融合算子组织。"
msgstr "Determine whether the output tile contains additional bias, scale, and activation. If the post-processing is lightweight, it can still be classified as a Cube operator; if the post-processing involves significant Vector reduction or cross-core synchronization, organize it as a CV fusion operator."

msgid "Cube 复杂算子开发"
msgstr "Developing complex operators for Cube."

msgid "复杂 Cube 场景通常来自 attention、batched matmul、grouped matmul 或形状不规则的矩阵乘。当前 [`Ascend/triton-ascend-ops`](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops) 主分支的复杂案例集中在 `tutorial/best_practice/`，其中 [`002-decode_grouped_attention.py`](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops/blob/main/tutorial/best_practice/002-decode_grouped_attention.py) 可以作为复杂 Cube 核心逻辑的参考：它包含 QK、PV 两段 `tl.dot`，并展示了 KV cache 离散索引下如何重组 K/V 访存。"
msgstr "Complex Cube scenarios typically originate from attention, batched matmul, grouped matmul, or matrix multiplication with irregular shapes. Currently, the complex cases on the main branch of [`Ascend/triton-ascend-ops`](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops) are concentrated in `tutorial/best_practice/`. Among them, [`002-decode_grouped_attention.py`](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops/blob/main/tutorial/best_practice/002-decode_grouped_attention.py) serves as a reference for complex Cube core logic. It contains two `tl.dot` segments for QK and PV, and demonstrates how to reorganize K/V memory access under discrete KV cache indexing."

msgid "复杂 Cube 算子建议按以下顺序拆解："
msgstr "For complex Cube operators, it is recommended to decompose them in the following order:"

msgid "**先抽出纯矩阵乘核心**：确认每次 `tl.dot` 的输入 tile shape、dtype、累加 dtype 和输出 tile shape。"
msgstr "**First extract the pure matrix multiplication core**: Confirm the input tile shape, dtype, accumulation dtype, and output tile shape for each `tl.dot`."

msgid "**再处理不规则访存**：如果 K/V cache 低维离散、高维连续，直接二维 load 可能退化为标量访存。可先按连续维搬入 UB，再通过转置或 Ascend 扩展接口 `extension.insert_slice` 重组为 `tl.dot` 需要的布局。"
msgstr "**Next, handle irregular memory access**: If the K/V cache is low-dimensional discrete and high-dimensional contiguous, a direct 2D load may degrade to scalar memory access. First, move the data to UB along the contiguous dimension. Then, reorganize the data into the layout required by `tl.dot` using transposition or the Ascend extension interface `extension.insert_slice`."

msgid "**把归约和归一化留到边界明确的位置**：例如 attention 中的 `max/sum/exp` 属于 Vector 逻辑，若和 `tl.dot` 放在同一 kernel，需要转到 [CV 融合算子开发](./cv_fusion_operator.md) 的思路。"
msgstr "**Leave reduction and normalization to positions with clear boundaries**: For example, `max/sum/exp` in attention belongs to Vector logic. If you place these operations in the same kernel as `tl.dot`, switch to the approach described in [CV Fusion Operator Development](./cv_fusion_operator.md)."

msgid "**为长 K 或长序列设计内层循环**：K 维循环要控制单次 A/B tile 的片上占用；序列维循环要避免一次 load 过大的 K/V block。"
msgstr "**Designing inner loops for long K or long sequences**: The K dimension loop must control the on-chip memory usage of a single A/B tile; the sequence dimension loop must avoid loading an oversized K/V block at once."

msgid "**用 Autotune 管理候选 tile**：为常见 shape 准备多组 `BLOCK_M/N/K` 和 `multibuffer` 配置，让运行时选择最优组合。"
msgstr "**Manage candidate tiles using Autotune**: Prepare multiple `BLOCK_M/N/K` and `multibuffer` configurations for common shapes. Allow the runtime to select the optimal combination."

msgid "复杂 Cube 算子的常见风险是把 GPU 上的大量 program 直接迁移到 NPU。对于逻辑核相互独立且通过 IR 安全分析的 kernel，后端会自动把逻辑 grid 映射到可用物理核；不适用的 kernel 会被自动跳过。如果 kernel 存在顺序依赖或未通过安全分析，应让每个 program 通过内层循环处理多个 tile。"
msgstr "A common risk with complex Cube operators is directly migrating a large number of programs from the GPU to the NPU. For kernels whose logical cores are independent of each other and pass IR safety analysis, the backend automatically maps the logical grid to available physical cores; kernels that are not applicable are automatically skipped. If a kernel has sequential dependencies or fails the safety analysis, each program should handle multiple tiles through an inner loop."
